ernment in Manipur and Arunachal Pradesh. JD(U), as part of the Bharatiya Janata Party-led National Democratic Alliance, won 12 seats in the 2024 Indian general election, making it the seventh largest party in the Lok Sabha.", "newValue": "Janata Dal (United) (JD(U)), established in 1999, is a prominent social democratic and secular political party in India, primarily active in the states of Bihar, Manipur, and Arunachal Pradesh. Its significance lies in its commitment to social justice and the upliftment of marginalized communities, positioning it as a critical player in the contemporary Indian political landscape. Influenced by leaders such as Nitish Kumar, who has served multiple terms as Chief Minister of Bihar, JD(U) has shaped regional politics by advocating for policies aimed at socio-economic development and empowerment of disadvantaged groups.

